# Proximi.io iOS Native WebView Demo

Native SwiftUI shell around a `WKWebView` that shows a Proximi.io web map and
feeds it the device position from the **Proximi.io iOS SDK v6** (Swift Package,
`import Proximiio`). Positions, floor changes and a simple accelerometer-based
"is moving" flag are posted to the page as:

    window.postMessage({ type: "SET_LOCATION", latitude, longitude, level,
                         accelAvailable, isInMovement }, "*")

## Usage

1. `cp Config/Secrets.example.xcconfig Config/Secrets.xcconfig` and set
   `PROXIMIIO_APPLICATION_TOKEN` and `PROXIMIIO_MAP_URL` (write the URL as
   `https:/$()/host/path` — `//` starts a comment in xcconfig). The file is
   gitignored; its values are baked into the Info.plist keys
   `ProximiioApplicationToken` / `ProximiioMapURL` at build time and read by
   `DemoConfiguration` at runtime. Without it the app shows a hint instead of
   crashing.
2. Open `ProximiioWebViewDemo.xcodeproj` and run on a device (positioning needs
   real Bluetooth / location / motion hardware).

The SDK is resolved by Swift Package Manager from
`https://github.com/proximiio/proximiio-ios-sdk-v6` (branch `master`). No
CocoaPods. To develop against a local SDK checkout, change the `Proximiio`
package in `project.yml` to `path: ../proximiio-ios-sdk-v6`.

## Project

`project.yml` (XcodeGen) is the source of truth; the checked-in
`ProximiioWebViewDemo.xcodeproj` is generated from it — after editing
`project.yml` run `xcodegen generate` (`brew install xcodegen`).

Info.plist usage descriptions are declared in `project.yml` (`info.properties`):
location when-in-use / always, Bluetooth (beacons) and Motion (pedestrian
dead-reckoning).

## SDK v6 flow (what replaced the 5.x delegate)

    let sdk = try Proximiio(configuration: ProximiioConfiguration(token: token))
    _ = await sdk.requestPermissions(always: false)
    _ = await sdk.requestMotionPermission()      // PDR needs Motion & Fitness
    try await sdk.authenticate()
    try await sdk.start()
    await sdk.enablePdr()                        // 5.x ProximiioPDRProcessor
    for await update in await sdk.positions()   { … }   // proximiioPositionUpdated
    for await change in await sdk.floorChanges() { … }  // proximiioFloorChanged

See the SDK's `MIGRATION.md` for the full 5.x → 6.0 mapping.
